window.docContents[129].resolve({"/rules/RG1003/#RG1003-rationale":{"contents":"A foundation label summarizes exactly which assumptions a result rests on. An unclassified axiom has no label, so no profile claim about the declaration can be true.\n\nThe three logical labels are Kernel-only (no axioms), Choice-Free (a subset of propext and Quot.sound) and Standard-Logical (additionally Classical.choice). A surface's claim in foundation_manifest.json is the upper bound; each declaration is labeled from its own exact axiom set.\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009RG1003: Unknown transitive axioms are forbidden","header":"Why it matters","id":"/rules/RG1003/#RG1003-rationale"},"/rules/RG2002/#RG2002-rationale":{"contents":"Coverage is only meaningful against a complete, exact classification. Silently ignoring an unknown key or an unclassified target would let modules escape the audit or let a typo change the claim.\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009RG2002: Configuration must classify the complete Lake surface","header":"Why it matters","id":"/rules/RG2002/#RG2002-rationale"},"/rules/RG3001/#RG3001-rationale":{"contents":"An execution account that silently skipped an unresolved path would overstate what the compiled program is known to run.\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009RG3001: Execution closure must have no unresolved paths","header":"Why it matters","id":"/rules/RG3001/#RG3001-rationale"}});